<task id="032" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>NDA upload → AI assessment → 3 outcomes (sign-as-is + e-sign stub / minor-edits + redline / review → submit-wizard pre-filled)</title>
    <phase>P3 Legal Front Door intake MVP</phase>
    <gate>blocked-until:031</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth-sensitive AI on the external plane (app-only, no OBO), new BFF endpoint group, shared external-access + AI surfaces, spans client (3-outcome UI) + BFF + JPS config; tags bff-api/auth — FULL per CLAUDE.md §8.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The CENTERPIECE — orchestrates classify→assess→map→branch across the agreement-review AI machine, an app-only broker re-host of an OBO-only pre-fill/analysis path, and a 3-outcome contract; high blast radius + auth-sensitive + ADR-013/§10 placement judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Auth-sensitive; touches the shared external-access BFF surface + AI PublicContracts; builds on 031's Front Door group; must not race another BFF editor (conflict-check with teams-app-r1).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>031</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, frontend, ai</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>
  <prompt>Build the FR-23 NDA AI assessment: a workforce-plane, entitlement-scoped, app-only (NO OBO) BFF endpoint POST /api/v1/external/legal-front-door/nda/assess that stages an uploaded NDA to SPE app-only, runs an AI compliance assessment against the Spaarke NDA Standard by REUSING the agreement-review Action ({overallRisk}) + DocumentClassifierHandler (NDA) + AppOnlyAnalysisService, maps overallRisk to one of three outcomes via ComposeSummaryPageGenerator.BuildRecommendation triage logic, and returns {outcome, message, redlineDocumentId?, prefill?}. Wire the client 3-outcome UI: (a) compliant → sign-as-is + e-sign STUB link; (b) minor → edit list + a MOCK/pending redline (real synthesis gated by SPIKE 033 — do NOT build the redline synthesizer here); (c) review → "Submit NDA request" button opening the 031 intake wizard PRE-FILLED from the uploaded doc.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. ASP.NET Minimal API endpoint groups (ADR-008 route-group filters, ADR-019 ProblemDetails), broker-only external auth (ADR-028 +A1/A3, no OBO), AI via the Services/Ai/PublicContracts facade (ADR-013/§10), SPE via SpeFileStore app-only (ADR-007), Fluent v9 + React 18 client (ADR-021).</role>
  <goal>An NDA uploaded by a workforce Front Door user is assessed and triaged to one of three outcomes: (a) fully compliant → "sign as is" message + an e-signature STUB link; (b) minor/low-risk → an edit list + a redline artifact reference (MOCK/pending — outcome-(b) synthesis is gated by SPIKE 033); (c) requires legal review → the 031 intake wizard opens pre-filled from the uploaded document. The endpoint POST /api/v1/external/legal-front-door/nda/assess runs app-only on the workforce-external plane (never OBO), returns {outcome: compliant|minor|review, message, redlineDocumentId?, prefill?}, and an unclassifiable/non-NDA document routes to manual (review) rather than a wrong outcome.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-23 (the amendment centerpiece): on NDA upload, run an AI compliance assessment against the Spaarke NDA Standard and return one of three outcomes each with a distinct next action (see spec.md lines 247-253). Grounded reuse: the triage classification is ~80% reuse — agreement-review.action.json returns {overallRisk: Low|Medium|High|Critical, flaggedSections[…]}; overallRisk maps almost verbatim (Low→sign-as-is, Medium→minor-edits, High/Critical→review); the disposition logic exists in ComposeSummaryPageGenerator.BuildRecommendation:90-102; NDA detection + (c) pre-fill reuse DocumentClassifierHandler (NDA) + AppOnlyAnalysisService (app-only MI path exists) + the pre-fill engine (MatterPreFillService/IWorkspacePrefillAi → PreFillResponse{fields,confidence,prefilledFields[]}); the Standard is NdaStandard KNW-011 (NdaStandardClauseProvider, 16 clauses B1-B16). Net-new: (1) the triage orchestrator + the external app-only endpoint; (2) outcome-(b) auto-redline is the genuinely novel/hard piece and is ADR-tensioned with the advisory-only posture — DO NOT build it here; it is MOCK/pending SPIKE 033; (3) OBO-decoupling — bytes-in (external SPE broker read) + email export need app-only variants. This task delivers (1) + the client 3-outcome UI + outcomes (a) and (c) fully, and (b) as a mock. 031 supplies the intake wizard the (c) pre-fill drives.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>infra/dataverse/actions/agreement-review.action.json (the review Action → {overallRisk, flaggedSections[…]} — REUSE as-is; the triage input)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/**/ComposeSummaryPageGenerator.cs:90-102 (BuildRecommendation — the triage/disposition logic to reuse for overallRisk→outcome mapping)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/**/DocumentClassifierHandler.cs (NDA classification)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/**/AppOnlyAnalysisService.cs (app-only classify/pre-fill — the no-OBO path to re-host)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/** (the AI facade — external endpoint consumes AI through here, ADR-013/§10; no AI-internal types leak to the external surface)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/NdaStandardEndpoints.cs + NdaStandardClauseProvider (Baseline NDA Standard KNW-011, clauses B1-B16)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/**/MatterPreFillService.cs / IWorkspacePrefillAi (PreFillResponse{fields,confidence,prefilledFields[]} — the (c) form pre-fill engine, OBO today → app-only re-host)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/** + Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerPrincipalResolver.cs + Api/Filters/CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter.cs (the external group + group filter to reuse; workforce-plane policy from task 024)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/**/SpeFileStore.cs (app-only SPE staging/download, ADR-007; key on documentId, no Graph pointer exposure)</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/** (the 031 typed-intake driver + Front Door module — mount the NDA upload + 3-outcome UI; drive the (c) pre-filled wizard)</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (binding BFF governance — Placement Justification + publish size)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>031 (typed-intake framework + MapFrontDoorEndpoints group + intake wizard) must be complete — outcome (c) opens that wizard pre-filled. 030 supplies sprk_servicerequest fields the (c) submission writes. 024 supplies the workforce-plane external-app auth policy the endpoint uses. Outcome-(b) real redline build is gated by SPIKE 033 (this task mocks it).</dependencies>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Broker-only: the NDA-assess endpoint runs on the workforce-external plane, app-only downstream (SPE + AI + Dataverse) — the caller token authenticates ONLY to the BFF and is NEVER exchanged for an OBO token. No OBO on any path in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Consume AI ONLY through Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ — do NOT inject IOpenAiClient / IPlaybookService / classifier internals or other AI-internal types into the external endpoint. No AI-internal type leaks to the external surface (§10 / refined ADR-013).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">All SPE reads/writes go through SpeFileStore app-only; authz-before-stream; key on documentId; never expose a Graph drive/item pointer to the client.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The endpoint is part of a route-group with a group-level authorization filter (reuse CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter under the Front Door group) — no per-endpoint ad-hoc middleware, no global middleware. ADR-019 ProblemDetails for all errors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Outcome (b) redline is MOCK/pending in R2 — return a placeholder redline reference (or an explicit "redline pending" marker) and DO NOT build a finding→edit synthesizer or call ComposeShadowPatchEngine to auto-apply redlines. The real (b) surface + artifact is gated by SPIKE 033 (spec.md line 253 ADR tension: agreement-review is advisory-only, MUST NOT auto-apply redlines).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">REUSE the existing NDA plumbing — do NOT author a new risk enum, a new NDA Standard, or a new triage rule set. Use agreement-review.action.json's {overallRisk} + BuildRecommendation's disposition + NdaStandard KNW-011 + DocumentClassifierHandler + AppOnlyAnalysisService (owner decision 2026-08-06).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF addition: state the Placement Justification in the PR (cite .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md); run dotnet publish -c Release and report compressed size + delta vs baseline 46.90 MB incl PDBs (ceiling ≤60 MB, escalate ≥+5 MB single-task); run /conflict-check before the BFF PR (teams-app-r1 shares Api/ExternalAccess/** + Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**; AI cluster shares Services/Ai/**).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Client 3-outcome UI in Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; zero hardcoded hex; verified light/dark/Teams theme + narrow Teams personal-tab width; dialogs via @spaarke/ui-components presets (no hand-rolled Dialog, §11/ADR-050).</constraint>
  </constraints>
