  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load spec.md FR-23 (lines 247-253) + review-additions-analysis.md item 1 + ADR-028/013/007/008/039 + bff-extensions.md. Read the reuse targets: agreement-review.action.json, ComposeSummaryPageGenerator.BuildRecommendation, DocumentClassifierHandler, AppOnlyAnalysisService, NdaStandardClauseProvider, MatterPreFillService/IWorkspacePrefillAi, the PublicContracts facade. Run /conflict-check for the external-access + AI BFF surfaces.</step>
    <step order="2">Author the NDA-intake extraction Action + one sprk_playbookconsumer binding row (zero executor code) for the outcome-(c) pre-fill (mirror how the workspace pre-fill Action is bound). Validate the JPS via jps-validate.</step>
    <step order="3">BFF: add POST /api/v1/external/legal-front-door/nda/assess under the Front Door group (031) with the group-level CallerPrincipalAuthorizationFilter on the workforce-plane external-app policy (024). App-only: stage the uploaded NDA via SpeFileStore (key on documentId), classify via DocumentClassifierHandler, assess via the agreement-review Action through the PublicContracts facade, and map {overallRisk} → outcome via reused BuildRecommendation disposition. ProblemDetails for errors.</step>
    <step order="4">BFF: build the outcome branches. (a) compliant → {outcome:"compliant", message, esignStubUrl}. (b) minor → {outcome:"minor", message, editList, redlineDocumentId: MOCK/pending} — DO NOT synthesize a real redline (gated by SPIKE 033); return a placeholder/"redline pending" marker. (c) review → {outcome:"review", message, prefill: PreFillResponse from the app-only pre-fill Action}. Unclassifiable/non-NDA → route to review (manual) — never emit a wrong compliant/minor outcome.</step>
    <step order="5">Client (external-spa): build the NDA upload + 3-outcome UI in the Front Door module. (a) render the sign-as-is message + the e-sign STUB link; (b) render the edit list + a MOCK redline download/email affordance (email reuses the FR-24 path; wire in 037); (c) render a "Submit NDA request" button that opens the 031 intake wizard PRE-FILLED from prefill. Fluent v9 tokens; presets only.</step>
    <step order="6">Tests: KEEP-path integration tests in tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ exercising the real endpoint-group wiring for all 3 outcomes + the unclassifiable→review negative + a no-OBO assertion (the endpoint never acquires an OBO token). NO Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; / DI-registration / ctor-null tests (ADR-038). Client component tests for the 3-outcome render + the (c) pre-filled wizard hand-off.</step>
    <step order="7">Build: npm run build:prod (client); dotnet publish -c Release — report compressed size + delta vs 46.90 MB. State the Placement Justification in the task notes / PR body.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅ completed.</step>
    <step order="9">Document deviations + the outcome-(b) mock boundary (what SPIKE 033 must resolve) in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If outcome (a) or (c) cannot be built app-only — i.e. any reused component (pre-fill, classifier, assessment, SPE read, or email export) requires an OBO/user token that has no app-only variant and cannot be re-hosted broker-only — STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required (NFR-01 / ADR-028: no OBO on any SPA path). Do NOT introduce OBO to make the assessment work. Present the specific component + the app-only gap + options (defer, new app-only variant, scope cut).</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test/publish the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Build/test the external-spa client (build:prod)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Shell, /conflict-check, jps-validate</tool>
  </tools>
  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/** — POST /api/v1/external/legal-front-door/nda/assess (app-only, workforce-plane, 3-outcome) + triage orchestrator via PublicContracts</output>
    <output type="code">infra/dataverse/actions/** — NDA-intake extraction Action + one sprk_playbookconsumer binding row (no executor code)</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/external-spa/** — NDA upload + 3-outcome UI; outcome-(c) pre-filled 031 wizard hand-off</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/** — 3-outcome + unclassifiable→review + no-OBO KEEP-path integration tests; client 3-outcome component tests</output>
  </outputs>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a fully-compliant NDA (agreement-review overallRisk=Low), when POST nda/assess runs, then it returns {outcome:"compliant", message, esignStubUrl} and the client shows the sign-as-is message + the e-sign STUB link.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a minor/low-risk NDA (overallRisk=Medium), when nda/assess runs, then it returns {outcome:"minor", message, editList, redlineDocumentId} where redlineDocumentId is a MOCK/pending marker (no real synthesized redline; 033 gates the real one) and the client shows the edit list + a download/email affordance.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a review-required NDA (overallRisk=High|Critical), when nda/assess runs, then it returns {outcome:"review", message, prefill} and the client opens the 031 intake wizard pre-filled from prefill.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (unclassifiable): given a non-NDA or unclassifiable document, when nda/assess runs, then it routes to outcome "review" (manual) — it NEVER returns "compliant" or "minor" for a document it could not assess.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative (no OBO): the endpoint runs app-only on the workforce-external plane — a test asserts no OBO/user token is acquired downstream (SPE + AI + Dataverse are all app-only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the endpoint consumes AI, when reviewed, then it depends ONLY on Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ types — no IOpenAiClient/classifier-internal type appears in the external endpoint (ADR-013/§10).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the BFF build, when dotnet publish -c Release runs, then compressed size is reported with delta vs 46.90 MB and is ≤60 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the 3-outcome UI, when rendered in light/dark/Teams theme at narrow width, then semantic tokens adapt with zero hardcoded hex and no console errors.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <justification>
    <existing>agreement-review.action.json + ComposeSummaryPageGenerator.BuildRecommendation:90-102 + DocumentClassifierHandler + AppOnlyAnalysisService + NdaStandardClauseProvider (KNW-011) + MatterPreFillService/IWorkspacePrefillAi already deliver classify + risk-assess + disposition + pre-fill — verified in review-additions-analysis.md item 1 (~80% reuse). What does NOT exist: an external-plane, app-only, workforce-scoped NDA-assess endpoint returning the 3-outcome contract; the existing pre-fill/analysis is OBO/workforce-only.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the AI machine (reuse the Action, disposition, classifier, Standard, pre-fill as-is via the PublicContracts facade); No for the endpoint (net-new external group route + triage orchestrator), because the OBO-only paths must be re-hosted broker-only/app-only — a genuine new surface justified by FR-23.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the app-only external endpoint + triage orchestrator, a workforce Front Door user cannot get an NDA assessed on the SPA (the OBO/core-user pre-fill/analysis path is unreachable from the external plane) — FR-23 (the amendment centerpiece) has no delivery, and every NDA falls back to manual legal review with no auto-fill.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Three outcomes render">
      <steps><step>Upload an NDA in the Front Door module</step><step>Exercise each outcome (compliant / minor / review) via seeded assessment results</step></steps>
      <expected>(a) sign-as-is + e-sign stub link; (b) edit list + mock redline affordance; (c) "Submit NDA request" opens the pre-filled 031 wizard; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark + Teams theme (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Toggle dark mode via ThemeToggle</step><step>Load inside a Teams-theme host (light/dark/high-contrast) at narrow width</step></steps>
      <expected>Zero hardcoded hex; tokens adapt across light/dark/Teams; readable at Teams personal-tab width</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Unclassifiable routes to review">
      <steps><step>Upload a non-NDA document</step></steps>
      <expected>Client shows the review outcome (manual) — never a compliant/minor result</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>
  <notes>Spec FR-23 (lines 247-253) — the amendment CENTERPIECE. Reuse ALL existing NDA plumbing (owner 2026-08-06). Outcome (b) redline is MOCK/pending — the real business-user redline surface + artifact is gated by SPIKE 033 (do NOT build the synthesizer here; it is ADR-tensioned with the advisory-only posture). §10 BFF: Placement Justification + publish size + conflict-check mandatory. No OBO on any path (ADR-028/A3); AI only via PublicContracts (ADR-013/§10). Use build:prod (NOT build) per CLAUDE.md §12 / AP-1.</notes>
